# Losing a conversation: the tree runs, a branch is walked, the resolution roll fails, and the
# tree's FAILURE branch is spoken instead.
#
# This is a DIALOGUE FEATURE test, not a test of the meet_stranger tree — that tree is only the
# cheapest one to reach. What it covers is the machinery every tree shares: the greeting, the reply
# options, the resolution check, and the outcomes landing on the NPC.
#
# Deliberately does NOT pass --auto-dialogue. That flag settles a conversation without holding one so
# a verb test can assert about its verb; here the conversation is the thing under test.
#
# It works at all because --playground now stubs DialogueTreeAdapter's LLM slot. Before that, Setup
# threw "Server is not ready", the dialogue "completed" instantly, and every tree in the game was
# unreachable under --playground — silently.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Reach the conversation through the verb that opens it — which must SUCCEED, or no conversation
# happens and there is nothing to lose. `strategy` is a preset consulted at every roll, and this
# script needs two different answers at two different moments: the verb's roll here, the dialogue's
# resolution roll further down. Setting fail-dice this early failed the verb instead, and the script
# then sat waiting for a Dialogue mode that was never coming.
strategy succeed
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The tree is live. `advance` drains whichever preview box is up — the NPC's greeting, then each
# reply option, which are generated as their own stack.
wait mode Dialogue 60

# NOW switch the preset: the conversation is open, and the roll under test is its resolution.
strategy fail-dice

advance 20 180
expect Good day
regions

# Walk a branch to its resolution. Two replies is the shortest route through this tree.
click option 0
advance 20 180
regions
click option 0
advance 20 180

# The resolution roll is settled; confirming it applies the branch's outcome.
click continue
advance 20 180

# The branch's SUCCESS replica, not its failure one — this is what tells the two apart, and so what
# proves the resolution roll was honoured rather than the tree merely reaching an end.
# The branch's FAILURE replica. The mirror of dialogue_success.cli: same tree, same branch,
# opposite roll — so between them they prove the resolution check decides the outcome.
expect Then keep walking
state
quit
